List and open cameras through the Camera portal and PipeWire on Linux

The video device opened cameras through V4L2 alone (/dev/video*), which a sandbox such
as a Flatpak's has only with every device of the computer. SetCameraPortal makes it take
WebRTC's other way instead, VideoCaptureOptions with PipeWire: RequestCameraAccess asks
xdg-desktop-portal's Camera interface (the person, or the permission they gave before)
once, and the cameras of the PipeWire connection it gives are listed and opened from then
on, coming and going as they are plugged in and out. GetCameraAccess tells whether they
were granted, refused or cannot be reached (no portal, no Camera interface, no PipeWire);
V4L2 stands in then if asked to (SetCameraPortal's direct_fallback), never after a
refusal. A camera PipeWire reaches through V4L2 keeps the id V4L2 gives it (its bus), so a
camera chosen before stays chosen. PipeWire is asked for exactly one of the formats the
camera offers, the nearest to the size and rate wanted (V4L2 picks its own). The device
name of a camera gone since it was counted is an error, not an empty name. Elsewhere,
and on Linux by default, nothing changes.

